{
  "_about": {
    "purpose": "Single 50-lead evaluation set covering scoring reliability (tier 1), scoring accuracy against a human gold set (tier 2), and adversarial robustness. Replaces three separate fixture lists.",
    "icp_assumed": "CrewAI multi-agent orchestration. Strong: operational scale + engineering function + a concrete automation use case + a technical/operational decision-maker, any vertical. Weak: very small or low-tech, no engineering function. Disqualified: ships or operates a competing agent-orchestration platform (NOT merely having AI features in the product).",
    "groups": {
      "accuracy": "Hand-score each 0-100 blind, then compare MAE / bias / within-10 / Spearman / confusion at 70.",
      "reliability": "Score each N times (default 10) to measure stdev, threshold straddling, and strong-vs-weak separation.",
      "sensitivity": "Same person and company, seniority changed. The score must fall when the title drops.",
      "invariance": "Cosmetic-only edits (case, padding). The score must not move.",
      "adversarial": "Pass/fail robustness checks rather than a numeric target."
    },
    "expect_values": "strong | borderline | weak | disqualified | adversarial",
    "notes": [
      "Person names are invented; company names are real, because the disqualifier and the scale signal are properties of the company. Emails use example.com.",
      "Mid-seniority leads use unresolvable invented names on purpose: web research cannot identify them, so the submitted title drives the score, which is what puts them near the 70 cutoff.",
      "adv_incomplete has empty required fields by design. It can be fed to the pipeline directly but cannot be bulk-imported through the CSV path, which validates them."
    ]
  },

